==English==

===Etymology===
The word ''telecommunication'' was adapted from the {{F.}} word ''télécommunication''. It is a compound of the Greek prefix ''tele-'' (τηλε-), meaning 'far off', and the Latin ''communicare'', meaning 'to share'.<ref>''Telecommunication'', ''tele-'' and ''communication'', [[New Oxford American Dictionary]] (2nd edition), 2005.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-}}

# the [[science]] and [[technology]] of [[communication]] at a [[distance]], especially the [[electronic]] [[transmission]] of [[signal]]s; [[telecommunication]]
# the [[system]]s used in transmitting such signals
# {{plural of|telecommunication}}

